athbf{b},$ $\\mathbf{c}$ be three vectors such that\n\\[\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]Compute $\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b}).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"ac5ef49306d7444461100232753035309998368e5c52da3dfc79255650337bae"},"seconds":41.79031276702881,"seed":355679781761115122,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to compute $\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b})$ given the cross products of the vectors $\\mathbf{a}, \\mathbf{b}, \\mathbf{c}$.\n\nFirst, we use the distributive property of the cross product. We have:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b}) = \\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a}) - \\mathbf{c} \\times (2 \\mathbf{b}).\n\\]\nUsing the scalar multiplication property of the cross product, we get:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a}) = 3 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}) \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\mathbf{c} \\times (2 \\mathbf{b}) = 2 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b}).\n\\]\nSince the cross product is anti-commutative, we have:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a} = - (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c}) \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b} = - (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}).\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n3 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}) = 3 (- (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c})) = -3 \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n2 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b}) = 2 (- (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})) = -2 \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -36 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nTherefore,\n\\[\n\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b}) = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -36 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 + 2 \\\\ -21 - 14 \\\\ -6 + 36 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
